Well, its finally done. Strange that I feel more relieved than actually
ecstatic at the accomplishment. I actually first started playing the
computer version of crack 10 years ago, give or take a month or two. It
seems somewhat fitting that it would happen now.

I will have to say that this is probably the luckiest game that I have
played to this point. An early shop yielded the speed boots, shield of
reflection and the oilskin cloak, the mines managed to produce two magic
lamps and GoDex off of separate bones piles on a single level, and the
lighting store in Minetown yielded yet another magic lamp (cross-aligned
altar though). With this early equipment boost and the Gnomish Mines'
seeming desire to pad my inventory with daggers off of the first two
levels, I was able to quickly get my dagger proficiency up to expert and
have a working stack of 40 daggers for enchantment and backup.

Gnomish mines went smoothly after I resurfaced to bless some water and
uncurse my lamps. First wish went to a blessed +3 GDSM which came down the
pipes in proper order in Minetown. I stashed the one lamp in my sack and
used the other for light and made my way. Also managed to identify a +3
ring of increase damage along the way, and it stayed on my finger most of
the game.

Nothing really noteworthy happened after the Mines until the Quest. The
Oracle level appeared on level 8 or so, and the Sokoban popped up on 10 -
I thought it was strange for these to be that deep, but really nothing to
get in a twist over. Sokoban coughed up a BoH that helped lighten the load
of my growing gem collection, and it was about when this was starting to
get out of hand that I used my second wish on a blessed touchstone. Not
exactly a power-wish, but I've always fancied that my first ascender
should be a "collector" of sorts and having a bag full of gems would fit
this bill.

After dumping the glass I continued descending until I crossed the on to
the Quest level. Not being high enough, I didn't even bother hitting the
home world yet. By the 20s (dungeon level) I had run across at least half
a dozen altars and the temple was co-aligned. Sac'ed for Stormy on one of
the lower levels altars and quickly got that up to expert. Just for the
fun of it, I two-weaponed for a while and got that up to expert as well,
but as it ends up I stayed single weapon with a shield of reflection
through the end, so that was somewhat of a moot point.

Had found enough scrolls of enchant armor and potions of water by the time
I hit the temple to get the daggers rustproofed and up to +5. I'd say that
this was probably the most pivotal point of the game. It made getting the
Master Key of Thievery incredibly easy, which is a fantastic artifact to
have with Stormbringer. I stashed most of the daggers, and kept them only
for the heaviest of combat - quest leaders, Rodneys, major demons, etc.

Castle yielded the usual results. Used two wishes on magic markers, one
for a wand of cancellation (I hadn't seen one yet and didn't want to goof
around with diluting potions and blanking scrolls by hand - far too time
consuming), and another for the helm of brilliance. Re-ascended to the
co-aligned temple to produce holy water and enchant my gear in safety, and
accidentally got Sting when I offered to test my prayer time-out. Burned
through a few wands of create monster get my timeout back, get the holy
water and fooproof and enchant my armor and main weapon.

Accidentally vaporized the GDSM and used another wish to get it back, and
it again was delivered blessed and +3 in short order. My jaw hit the
floor, but I didn't stick around to ask questions. I descended and dove
through the castle traps to get the the gates of Gehennom (accidentally
attacking and killing the priest in the process). First step through the
gates I realized I had forgotten the candles in Minetown. Damnit...

After their collection, I stopped back in the lower temple to see about
getting crowned, but all I got was this lousy Fire Brand instead.

Again, I didn't press the issue. Worked my way through Gehennom, using the
collected wands of digging to cut a path of least resistance between the
stairs and fully explored each level looking for gems. The major demons
and Vlad fell easily to a barrage of daggers, and since I hadn't
identified a ring of levitation yet, I used the last wish from the wand to
get a blessed one of those. Rodney dropped easily as well, but I killed
him over the water, so I had to backtrack again to find a wand of cold to
get the Book of the Dead.

Moseyed over to the vibrating square and set about doing the ritual. First
time it flopped.... I had forgotten to light the Candelabrum. Being
annoyed and not paying attention, I managed to flub the second attempt
too. Lit the candelabra, read from the book then rang the bell. *smacks
forehead* Third time worked like a charm though. I donned the =oConflict
that made Rodney's graveyards easy and worked my way through to Moloch's
High Priest. Grabbed the amulet and started the mad dash. Only had to deal
with level warpage one time all the way to the endgame. Again... a jaw
dropper.

Having previously had my ass handed to me in short order on the Plane of
Air (my 3 previous demi-god hopefuls bit it here), I was almost
disgruntled whenever I practically waltzed my way through ALL of the
Planes. Stormbringer, the Master Key and conflict are really a ruthless
combination. I didn't have to use a single potion of full healing or an
AoLS. Honestly, the only major scare I had was when I came close to
starving after fighting Famine. My health on the last level dropped as low
as 80 or so, but never any lower.

Was it stylish? Not terribly. I used 8 wishes total and genocided 3
species. I didn't even manage to complete my dragon scale collection. Next
ascension will be genoless though. Maybe even vegetarian too. At least
there's a pretty big bag of rocks to gamble with at the Demi-god bar and
casino.


